WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:19.239
When I married, I moved out of the Baker Street rooms that I shared with Sherlock Holmes.

2
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.382
At first the great detective continued to call upon me when he needed someone to accompany him on

3
00:00:24.442 --> 00:00:25.362
his investigations.

4
00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:29.224
But as the years passed, those occasions became less frequent.

5
00:00:30.152 --> 00:00:35.016
I’d recently read in the newspapers that Holmes was working on an important matter for the French government.

6
00:00:35.777 --> 00:00:39.660
So you can imagine my surprise when he suddenly appeared in my study one April evening.

7
00:00:41.181 --> 00:00:43.883
I immediately noticed that he looked quite pale and thin.

8
00:00:43.903 --> 00:00:44.824
“Yes, Dr.

9
00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:48.987
Watson, your observations are correct,” he said in response to my concerned glance.

10
00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.269
“I’ve been under some strain lately.

11
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.611
Do you mind if I close the shutters over your window?”

12
00:00:55.693 --> 00:00:59.176
Before I could reply, he edged around the room and bolted the shutters securely.

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.341
The only light in the room came from a lamp near the chair where I had been reading.

14
00:01:03.361 --> 00:01:05.402
“You’re afraid of something?”

15
00:01:05.922 --> 00:01:06.343
I asked.

16
00:01:06.363 --> 00:01:08.984
“An air gun,” he replied.

17
00:01:09.004 --> 00:01:11.985
“My dear Holmes, what are you talking about?”

18
00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:16.247
“I think you know me well enough, Watson, to understand that I’m not a nervous man.”

19
00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:18.047
Holmes stepped closer.

20
00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:22.549
“However, I would be stupid to refuse to recognize danger when it’s nearby.”

21
00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.351
Holmes held out his hand, and I saw that two knuckles were bleeding.

22
00:01:26.371 --> 00:01:28.112
“You’ve been in a fight!”

23
00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:29.052
I cried.

24
00:01:29.984 --> 00:01:32.346
“Yes, I’m involved in something quite serious.”

25
00:01:33.607 --> 00:01:38.010
Holmes’ eyes shone with the familiar excitement that meant he was deeply absorbed in a case.

26
00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:40.511
“Is Mrs.

27
00:01:40.551 --> 00:01:41.152
Watson at home?”

28
00:01:42.012 --> 00:01:44.414
“No, she’s away for a few days visiting a relative.”

29
00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:48.617
“Good! Then it’s easier for me to propose that you join me for a week away.”

30
00:01:48.637 --> 00:01:50.058
“Where are we going?”

31
00:01:50.078 --> 00:01:51.799
“Oh, anywhere.

32
00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:53.220
It’s all the same to me.”

33
00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:58.644
“This is very strange,” I thought as I fetched a basin of water and a cloth for his

34
00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:04.480
hand. It wasn’t like Holmes to take aimless vacations, and something about his face suggested that his nerves

35
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.621
were at the breaking point.

36
00:02:06.742 --> 00:02:09.405
After Holmes cleaned up his injury, he took a seat facing me.

37
00:02:09.425 --> 00:02:12.167
“Have you ever heard of Professor Moriarty?”

38
00:02:12.928 --> 00:02:17.111
Holmes leaned forward, putting his fingertips together and resting his elbows on his knees.

39
00:02:18.493 --> 00:02:19.153
I shook my head.

40
00:02:19.173 --> 00:02:22.056
“You’re not alone, Watson.

41
00:02:23.037 --> 00:02:26.460
He’s one of the most influential men in London, and yet no one has heard of him.

42
00:02:27.624 --> 00:02:31.206
If I could free society from that man, it would be the peak of my career.

43
00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:34.208
Then I could retire to a quieter line of work.”

44
00:02:35.669 --> 00:02:36.269
“What has he done?”

45
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:43.873
Holmes told me that Moriarty had been an unusually brilliant, prize-winning mathematics professor at a small university outside

46
00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:50.357
London. However, when rumors of criminal activity swirled around him, he had to resign his position.

47
00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:55.560
“As you are aware, Watson, no one knows the London criminal world as well as I do.

48
00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.663
For years I’ve been conscious of a link between all sorts of cases—forgeries, robberies, murders.

49
00:03:02.964 --> 00:03:05.645
But I could never figure out what the link was until now.”

50
00:03:07.246 --> 00:03:11.368
Holmes explained that Moriarty was the mastermind behind the worst crimes in the city.

51
00:03:11.388 --> 00:03:14.710
“The professor never actually participates in the crimes.

52
00:03:15.791 --> 00:03:20.053
Instead he commands a whole network of people who carry out his diabolical plans.

53
00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:24.516
He’s like the spider that waits quietly in the center of the web.”

54
00:03:25.396 --> 00:03:27.017
“What happens when his people get caught?”

55
00:03:27.478 --> 00:03:27.918
I asked.

56
00:03:28.518 --> 00:03:31.821
“Don’t they tell the police about Moriarty in an attempt to save themselves?”

57
00:03:31.841 --> 00:03:36.304
“Whenever someone is caught, money quickly appears for bail or a lawyer.

58
00:03:37.345 --> 00:03:39.487
No one ever suspects Moriarty is behind it all.”

59
00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:42.849
Holmes had pursued the professor for three months.

60
00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.993
Every time he had been about to close in on Moriarty, the genius managed to escape.

61
00:03:49.154 --> 00:03:51.976
Holmes was forced to admit that he had met his intellectual equal.

62
00:03:54.592 --> 00:03:57.093
But recently Moriarty had made a tiny mistake.

63
00:03:58.253 --> 00:04:03.394
Holmes did not explain what that was, saying only that on Monday, three days from now, the professor

64
00:04:03.474 --> 00:04:05.515
and his main gang members would be arrested.

65
00:04:05.535 --> 00:04:11.777
“There’s enough evidence to convict them of more than forty crimes,” Holmes said with a look of satisfaction.

66
00:04:11.797 --> 00:04:15.078
“It’ll be the criminal trial of the century.”

67
00:04:15.098 --> 00:04:17.558
“Don’t you want to be around to see that?”

68
00:04:17.918 --> 00:04:18.339
I asked.

69
00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:20.899
“Are you sure you want to leave London?”

70
00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:25.413
“That’s a recent decision—made early this morning, as a matter of fact.”

71
00:04:26.454 --> 00:04:27.695
Holmes gave me a bitter laugh.

72
00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:34.260
“I was sitting in my study in my dressing gown, thinking over the case, when the door opened

73
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.081
and Professor Moriarty stood before me.”

74
00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:39.743
I gasped and Holmes said he’d been surprised too.

75
00:04:39.764 --> 00:04:44.907
“I was familiar with the professor’s appearance, but it was startling to see him in the flesh.”

76
00:04:46.028 --> 00:04:51.392
Holmes explained that Moriarty was extremely tall and thin with sunken eyes and a clean-shaven face.

77
00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:54.857
He had peered at Holmes with great curiosity.

78
00:04:55.978 --> 00:05:00.781
“Moriarty smiled,” Holmes went on, “but there was something in his eyes that made me wish that I

79
00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.102
had my revolver close by.”

80
00:05:03.182 --> 00:05:06.044
I found the rest of Holmes’ story fascinating and frightening.

81
00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:09.066
Holmes had beckoned for Moriarty to take a seat.

82
00:05:09.086 --> 00:05:13.088
“If you have anything to say, Professor, I can spare you five minutes.”

83
00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:18.692
As Moriarty sat down, he reached into his pocket, and Holmes feared that he was reaching for a

84
00:05:18.732 --> 00:05:22.733
gun. But Moriarty pulled out a notebook in which he’d scribbled some dates.

85
00:05:24.953 --> 00:05:28.775
“You crossed my path on January 4,” Moriarty read aloud.

86
00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:31.695
“On January 23 you bothered me.

87
00:05:32.516 --> 00:05:35.756
By the middle of February, I was seriously inconvenienced by you.

88
00:05:36.837 --> 00:05:41.278
At the end of March, you ruined my plans, and now in April, I find that I am

89
00:05:41.318 --> 00:05:43.899
in danger of losing my liberty, thanks to you.

90
00:05:45.079 --> 00:05:46.679
This situation has become impossible.

91
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.360
You must give up.”

92
00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.061
“After Monday,” Holmes said.

93
00:05:51.081 --> 00:05:57.025
“It’s been an intellectual treat for me to see how you’ve grappled with this affair,” Moriarty said.

94
00:05:57.045 --> 00:06:01.688
“A man with your brain should be able to see that there can be only one outcome.

95
00:06:02.949 --> 00:06:05.791
It would distress me to have to take an extreme measure against you.”

96
00:06:07.392 --> 00:06:08.873
Holmes was unbothered by the threat.

97
00:06:08.893 --> 00:06:12.495
“I long ago accepted that danger is a part of my profession.”

98
00:06:12.515 --> 00:06:15.677
“This is not danger!”

99
00:06:16.118 --> 00:06:16.918
Moriarty snapped.

100
00:06:16.938 --> 00:06:19.200
“It’s inevitable destruction.

101
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.903
You stand in the way not merely of an individual but also of a mighty organization, the full

102
00:06:24.943 --> 00:06:27.125
extent of which you cannot comprehend.”

103
00:06:28.286 --> 00:06:28.966
Holmes stood up.

104
00:06:29.987 --> 00:06:33.389
“This has been a pleasant conversation, but I’m neglecting important business elsewhere.”

105
00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.472
Shaking his head sadly, Moriarty looked at Holmes in silence.

106
00:06:38.473 --> 00:06:40.714
“Well, it’s a pity,” the professor said at last.

107
00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.336
“I’ve done what I could to warn you.

108
00:06:44.357 --> 00:06:47.879
Even if you’re clever enough to kill me, rest assured that one of my men will do the

109
00:06:47.899 --> 00:06:48.440
same to you.

110
00:06:49.344 --> 00:06:50.746
He already has my instructions.”
